  "_note": "Resources are stackable and never consume an inventory slot. Motes are the Reality-layer currency and bank into RealityState, not BaseState. 'drivenBy' names the pressure target whose magnitude sets how much of this a world holds; 'requires' are conditions without which there is none at all; 'favours' each multiply its share. THE DESIGN RULE (resources-skills-spec §1): every resource should make you want to write a particular kind of world — if two come from the same conditions, one is redundant. Which is why the exotic ones are gated behind 'requires' rather than merely favoured: an ordinary world still pays ore and fibre, and mercury is something you go and write for. 'ore' keeps its id (it is a research cost and a save key) and is the workhorse metal the spec calls Iron; a separate iron would be the same thing twice. All PLACEHOLDER.",
